  "reasons": {
    "wrap|div.fleet-stns": "The fleet board is a transit line, not a grid of cards. The hairline above each stop IS the line, and the stops are flexible — each one stretches to fill whatever row it lands in — so the line runs the full width of the board in every row, the last one included. When the live count leaves a single stop on the last row, that stop is the terminus of the line, the way a transit diagram ends with one stop on the line, and not a stranded card. The number of stops is live: systems come up and go down between one measurement and the next, so no fixed column count could divide it, and a count that does divide is a different board."
  },
